  "summary": "Package exfiltrates host and environment data to hardcoded Telegram bot endpoint",
  "details": "The package @inetafrica/open-claudia@3.1.22 contains multiple modules that pair filesystem/process/host reconnaissance with outbound HTTPS to a hardcoded Telegram Bot API endpoint (api.telegram.org). setup.js and health.js import child_process, fs, and https, read process.env, process.platform, process.version, and host identifiers, and POST/GET to https://api.telegram.org, indicating a Telegram-bot C2/exfiltration channel. bot.js, core/handlers.js, core/media.js, and bin/cli.js exhibit the same child_process + http.request/https + hostname + process.env composition, and core/scheduler.js invokes spawn(\"sh\"). health.js and setup.js run on install/startup paths and beacon host identity out to the hardcoded Telegram endpoint, giving the publisher a persistent out-of-band channel to receive installer host and environment data.",
